<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33070" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orthō^grăphĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθογραφία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Orthography</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orthographia, id est formula ratioque scribendi
					a grammaticis instituta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 88</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Gram. 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 4, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 7,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In architecture, <i>an elevation</i>, <i>front view</i> of a building, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 1,
			2</span></i>.</div>
